-- Entirely fictional NovaTech Solutions policies for development/testing only.
-- Not real employer policies, legal guidance, or predefined question/answer pairs.
-- Only inserts missing records. Existing rows are never updated or deleted.
-- Natural seed identity: (category, title, source_name).
-- Use one connection for the entire file. The named lock serializes cooperating
-- seed executions. If the lock cannot be acquired, the INSERT inserts zero rows.
USE chatbot_db;
SET NAMES utf8mb4 COLLATE utf8mb4_unicode_ci;
SET @novatech_seed_lock = GET_LOCK('chatbot_db.novatech_knowledge_seed_001', 30);
START TRANSACTION;

INSERT INTO company_knowledge
    (category, title, content, keywords, source_name, source_url,
     department, access_level, is_active)
SELECT seed.category, seed.title, seed.content, seed.keywords, seed.source_name,
       NULL, seed.department, 'employee', 1
FROM (
    SELECT 'IT Support' AS category,
        'Company Password Reset' AS title,
        'Synthetic NovaTech Solutions policy. Employees should use the Password and Account Recovery section of the NovaTech Employee Portal to reset a forgotten company password after completing identity verification. An employee unable to enter the portal should contact the NovaTech IT Service Desk through the contact information in the employee welcome pack or company directory. The Service Desk verifies identity using an approved recovery method before initiating a reset. Managers cannot approve bypassing identity verification. After resetting, update saved credentials on managed devices and reconnect affected applications. Never send passwords or recovery codes in a ticket. Suspected account compromise must also be reported through the NovaTech Security Portal.' AS content,
        'password, forgotten password, reset password, locked account, account recovery, login trouble, credentials' AS keywords,
        'NovaTech Account Recovery Standard (Synthetic)' AS source_name,
        'IT' AS department
    UNION ALL SELECT 'IT Support', 'Company Laptop Replacement',
        'Synthetic NovaTech Solutions policy. Employees experiencing laptop hardware failure or damage should open a Hardware Support ticket with the NovaTech IT Service Desk. Include the asset tag, symptoms, business impact, and any safe diagnostic steps already attempted. The Service Desk diagnoses the device and decides whether repair or replacement is appropriate. Standard replacements require IT approval, and nonstandard equipment also requires manager budget approval. A loan device may be offered subject to availability. Back up work to approved company storage and arrange return of the old device before disposal or reassignment. Do not buy replacement equipment independently. Lost or stolen devices follow the security reporting process rather than ordinary hardware replacement.',
        'laptop, computer, broken laptop, hardware failure, replacement, damaged computer, loaner, asset tag',
        'NovaTech IT Equipment Support Policy (Synthetic)', 'IT'
    UNION ALL SELECT 'IT Support', 'Company VPN Troubleshooting',
        'Synthetic NovaTech Solutions policy. Employees should connect to company resources using the approved VPN client on an enrolled company device. For connection failures, confirm internet access, restart the client, check automatic device time, and review the service-status notice in the NovaTech Employee Portal. Complete only an MFA request triggered by the current sign-in attempt. Do not disable endpoint protection or install an alternative VPN client. If the issue continues, submit a Network Connectivity ticket to the NovaTech IT Service Desk with the error text, device asset tag, approximate failure time, and whether all or only some resources are affected. Never attach credentials, recovery codes, or unredacted connection logs containing secrets.',
        'VPN, remote connection, cannot connect, network, connection failed, tunnel, work from home, connectivity',
        'NovaTech Remote Connectivity Guide (Synthetic)', 'IT'
    UNION ALL SELECT 'IT Support', 'Software Installation Requests',
        'Synthetic NovaTech Solutions policy. Employees should first check the managed software catalog in the NovaTech Employee Portal for approved applications. If the application is unavailable, submit a Software Request ticket to the NovaTech IT Service Desk with the product name, business purpose, required features, intended users, and any purchase estimate. IT checks compatibility and licensing, and Information Security reviews software that handles company data or introduces new integrations. Paid software requires manager budget approval before purchase. Installation is performed through managed deployment or an authorized IT technician. Employees must not use personal licenses, bypass administrator controls, or download unapproved installers while a request is pending.',
        'software, install app, installation, program, administrator rights, license, approved software, software catalog',
        'NovaTech Software Approval Standard (Synthetic)', 'IT'
    UNION ALL SELECT 'IT Support', 'IT Help Desk Escalation',
        'Synthetic NovaTech Solutions policy. The NovaTech IT Service Desk provides routine support Monday through Friday from 08:00 to 18:00 in the employee office time zone, excluding local company holidays. Employees should create one ticket per issue and include the business impact and any deadline. Routine requests receive an initial response within one business day, which is not a resolution guarantee. If there is no response within that period, reply to the existing ticket and ask for escalation to the Service Desk lead. For a work-stopping outage during support hours, use the urgent contact listed in the company directory and quote the ticket number. Suspected security incidents use the NovaTech Security Portal immediately, including outside support hours.',
        'help desk, service desk, escalation, support ticket, no response, urgent IT, outage, support hours',
        'NovaTech IT Service Desk Operating Guide (Synthetic)', 'IT'
    UNION ALL SELECT 'Information Security', 'Lost or Stolen Company Device',
        'Synthetic NovaTech Solutions policy. Employees must immediately report a lost or stolen company laptop, phone, or storage device in the NovaTech Security Portal. The security reporting channel is monitored at all times. If the portal is inaccessible, use the urgent security contact in the employee welcome pack or company directory and ask a manager to help reach Information Security if needed. Provide the asset tag if known, last known location, approximate loss time, and whether the device was unlocked. Do not delay reporting while searching. Information Security coordinates account protection, remote lock or wipe, and any required external reporting. The NovaTech IT Service Desk handles replacement only after security triage. Employees must not attempt personal recovery from a suspected thief.',
        'lost laptop, stolen phone, missing device, theft, lost computer, remote wipe, device loss',
        'NovaTech Lost Device Response Procedure (Synthetic)', 'Information Security'
    UNION ALL SELECT 'Information Security', 'Phishing Email Reporting',
        'Synthetic NovaTech Solutions policy. Employees should use the Report Phishing control in the managed email application for suspicious messages. If that control is unavailable, report the message through the NovaTech Security Portal using an approved message attachment that preserves headers. Do not click links, open attachments, reply, or forward the message to coworkers. If a link was opened, credentials were entered, or a suspicious attachment was executed, report those facts immediately as a security incident. Include the approximate time and affected device without copying passwords or sensitive message contents into unrelated tickets. Information Security evaluates the report and coordinates cleanup. Employees should follow its instructions before deleting evidence.',
        'phishing, suspicious email, scam email, malicious link, report email, email headers, suspicious attachment',
        'NovaTech Suspicious Email Handling Standard (Synthetic)', 'Information Security'
    UNION ALL SELECT 'Information Security', 'Multi-Factor Authentication Recovery',
        'Synthetic NovaTech Solutions policy. Employees with a new phone, an unavailable authenticator, or repeated MFA errors should contact the NovaTech IT Service Desk for identity-verified MFA recovery. If a previously enrolled recovery method is available, it may be used through the NovaTech Employee Portal according to the displayed recovery steps. The Service Desk must verify identity before removing or replacing an authentication factor. A manager request alone is not sufficient, and MFA must not be disabled as a workaround. Never share one-time codes, recovery codes, or approval prompts with support staff. Unexpected approval requests must be denied and reported immediately through the NovaTech Security Portal. A lost company phone also requires the lost-device reporting process.',
        'MFA, two factor, 2FA, authenticator, new phone, verification code, push approval, recovery code',
        'NovaTech MFA Enrollment and Recovery Standard (Synthetic)', 'Information Security'
    UNION ALL SELECT 'Information Security', 'Security Incident Reporting',
        'Synthetic NovaTech Solutions policy. Employees must promptly report suspected malware, unauthorized account use, accidental disclosure, unusual access, or other security incidents through the NovaTech Security Portal. This channel is monitored at all times. If it is unavailable, use the urgent security contact in the company directory or welcome pack. State what happened, when it happened, the affected systems, and whether activity is continuing. Do not investigate independently, delete evidence, reset a device, or contact an external party without direction. If active malicious behavior is visible, disconnect the device from networks when safe and contact Information Security from a different trusted device. Information Security leads containment, investigation, and decisions about notifications.',
        'security incident, breach, malware, suspicious activity, account compromise, data leak, unauthorized access',
        'NovaTech Security Incident Response Procedure (Synthetic)', 'Information Security'
    UNION ALL SELECT 'HR', 'Paid Time Off Entitlement',
        'Synthetic NovaTech Solutions policy. In this fictional baseline policy, full-time employees receive 20 working days, equivalent to 160 hours, of paid time off per calendar year. Part-time schedules and midyear starts are prorated by HR. PTO covers vacation and planned personal time, while sick leave uses a separate balance. The NovaTech Employee Portal displays the applicable balance and any contract-specific terms. Up to five unused working days may carry into the next calendar year and must be used by March 31, unless an applicable employment agreement or local requirement provides otherwise. Employees should ask HR to resolve balance discrepancies before submitting leave. PTO availability does not replace manager approval of requested dates.',
        'PTO, paid time off, annual leave, leave balance, vacation allowance, accrual, carryover, holiday entitlement',
        'NovaTech Paid Time Off Policy (Synthetic)', 'HR'
    UNION ALL SELECT 'HR', 'Sick Leave and Absence Notification',
        'Synthetic NovaTech Solutions policy. Full-time employees have a separate baseline sick-leave allowance of 10 working days, equivalent to 80 hours, per calendar year. HR confirms part-time, joining-year, employment-agreement, and locally required provisions. Employees should notify their manager before the normal start time when practicable and record the absence in the Sick Leave section of the NovaTech Employee Portal within two working days of returning. If unable to report personally, a trusted contact may notify the manager. Send any requested medical documentation privately to HR rather than a team chat or IT ticket. For longer absences or an exhausted balance, contact HR to discuss the applicable leave process instead of automatically using PTO.',
        'sick leave, illness, unwell, medical absence, sick day, absence notification, doctor note',
        'NovaTech Sick Leave Procedure (Synthetic)', 'HR'
    UNION ALL SELECT 'HR', 'Vacation Request and Approval Process',
        'Synthetic NovaTech Solutions policy. Employees should request planned vacation in the Time Off section of the NovaTech Employee Portal at least 10 business days before the proposed start date. Check the PTO balance and discuss coverage with the manager before submission. Requests include dates, hours or partial days, and a handover plan without unnecessary personal details. Managers should respond within three business days and consider staffing, existing approvals, and operational needs. If no response arrives, follow up with the manager, then HR for workflow assistance. A submitted request is not approved leave, and employees should not make nonrefundable bookings before approval. Changes or cancellations must be recorded in the portal. Short-notice requests require explicit manager agreement.',
        'vacation, book leave, time off request, annual leave request, manager approval, holiday booking, handover',
        'NovaTech Vacation Scheduling Procedure (Synthetic)', 'HR'
    UNION ALL SELECT 'HR', 'Employee Benefits Information and Enrollment',
        'Synthetic NovaTech Solutions policy. The Benefits section of the NovaTech Employee Portal contains the current benefit summary, eligibility rules, plan documents, and enrollment instructions for the employee location and employment type. Offerings may include health coverage, retirement contributions, and employee assistance, but the applicable plan documents determine actual coverage. New employees should review their options and submit elections within 30 calendar days of their start date. Employees with a qualifying life event should contact HR within 30 calendar days to confirm the relevant enrollment process and documentation. Existing employees receive annual enrollment dates through the portal. Benefit questions and dependent information should be sent privately to HR, not to the IT Service Desk.',
        'benefits, health insurance, retirement, enrollment, dependent coverage, employee assistance, life event',
        'NovaTech Benefits Enrollment Guide (Synthetic)', 'HR'
    UNION ALL SELECT 'Application Access', 'Requesting Business Application Access',
        'Synthetic NovaTech Solutions policy. Employees request business application access through the NovaTech Access Portal. Select the application and required role, explain the business task, name the approving manager, and provide an end date for temporary access. The manager confirms the need, and the application owner approves the role based on least privilege and any separation-of-duties restrictions. Access is provisioned only after all required approvals. New software not listed in the catalog first follows the software approval process with the NovaTech IT Service Desk. Requests do not grant access automatically, and shared accounts are prohibited unless specifically approved and managed by IT. Employees should track request status in the portal rather than sending credentials through tickets.',
        'application access, app permission, request access, role, entitlement, business system, access denied, approval',
        'NovaTech Application Access Request Standard (Synthetic)', 'IT'
    UNION ALL SELECT 'Application Access', 'Changing or Removing Application Access',
        'Synthetic NovaTech Solutions policy. Managers must submit application-role changes and removals through the NovaTech Access Portal before a planned team transfer or employment end date when practicable. Include the effective date, affected applications, roles to remove, and any replacement responsibilities. Employees may request removal of their own unnecessary access at any time. Application owners review changed roles and IT records completion in the portal. Temporary access should expire on its approved end date rather than remain indefinitely. HR coordinates departure notifications with IT, and managers must not transfer an employee account to another person. Suspected inappropriate access or an urgent termination-related security concern must be reported immediately through the NovaTech Security Portal for expedited handling.',
        'remove access, change permissions, revoke role, team transfer, offboarding, access review, temporary access',
        'NovaTech Access Change and Revocation Procedure (Synthetic)', 'IT'
    UNION ALL SELECT 'Finance', 'Expense Reimbursement Submission',
        'Synthetic NovaTech Solutions policy. Employees submit eligible business expenses through the NovaTech Expense Portal within 30 calendar days of the expense date. Include an itemized receipt, business purpose, expense date, currency, cost center, and any required prior approval. The manager checks business necessity and budget, then Finance reviews policy compliance. Approved claims are normally paid within 10 business days after Finance approval, subject to the payment calendar shown in the portal. If a receipt is missing, use the missing-receipt declaration and obtain manager approval, which does not guarantee reimbursement. Personal purchases and duplicate claims are not reimbursable. For late claims or an unexplained rejection, request Finance review through the existing claim rather than submitting a duplicate.',
        'expense, reimbursement, receipt, claim, refund, business purchase, payment status, missing receipt',
        'NovaTech Business Expense Reimbursement Policy (Synthetic)', 'Finance'
    UNION ALL SELECT 'Finance', 'Business Travel Approval and Expenses',
        'Synthetic NovaTech Solutions policy. Employees must obtain manager approval and a cost estimate in the NovaTech Expense Portal before booking business travel. International travel also requires Finance approval before booking. Use the approved booking option shown in the portal, select economy transport and a standard hotel room, and check destination-specific spending limits before purchase. Meals, ground transport, and lodging must have a documented business purpose and itemized receipts. Personal extensions and companion costs are paid personally and separated from company claims. Submit travel expenses within 30 calendar days of each expense date under the reimbursement process. Changes outside approved limits require renewed approval. Finance reviews exceptions before a nonrefundable commitment whenever practicable.',
        'travel expense, business trip, airfare, hotel, meals, transport, travel approval, booking, international travel',
        'NovaTech Business Travel and Expense Standard (Synthetic)', 'Finance'
    UNION ALL SELECT 'Employee Onboarding', 'New Employee Technology Setup',
        'Synthetic NovaTech Solutions policy. Before a new employee starts, the hiring manager submits a New Starter request to the NovaTech IT Service Desk at least five business days before the start date, listing work location, equipment, and required applications. IT prepares a managed laptop and an account activation process. On the first working day, the employee follows identity verification, activates the account, enrolls MFA, confirms managed-device updates, and tests email and approved remote connectivity with IT assistance. Business application roles still require approval through the NovaTech Access Portal. Employees should report missing equipment or activation failures to the Service Desk and never use a coworker account while waiting. Managers coordinate delays with HR.',
        'new starter, technology setup, first day laptop, account activation, new hire equipment, onboarding IT',
        'NovaTech New Starter Technology Checklist (Synthetic)', 'IT'
    UNION ALL SELECT 'Employee Onboarding', 'First-Week Employee Onboarding',
        'Synthetic NovaTech Solutions policy. During the first week, new employees complete the onboarding checklist in the NovaTech Employee Portal with their manager and HR. The first day includes identity and employment-document checks through approved HR channels, team introductions, and the technology setup appointment with IT. By the end of the first week, employees should complete assigned security awareness training, review workplace and leave policies, confirm required application requests, and agree initial responsibilities with their manager. Benefits elections follow the separate 30-calendar-day enrollment window rather than a first-week deadline. Employees should tell HR about inaccessible tasks or unavailable documents so an alternative can be arranged. Personal identity documents must not be attached to general IT tickets.',
        'onboarding, first week, orientation, induction, new employee checklist, security training, new hire',
        'NovaTech First-Week Onboarding Guide (Synthetic)', 'HR'
    UNION ALL SELECT 'Workplace Policy', 'Remote and Hybrid Work Arrangements',
        'Synthetic NovaTech Solutions policy. Eligible roles may use a manager-approved hybrid arrangement with three office days and two remote days per working week. The manager records agreed days and role-specific exceptions in the NovaTech Employee Portal, and employees should request schedule changes before the affected week. Normal availability follows the agreed work schedule, with team collaboration hours from 10:00 to 15:00 in the team office time zone, excluding approved breaks. Remote work must use a managed device, approved connectivity, and a private setting that protects company information. Working from another country requires advance HR and Information Security approval. Hybrid eligibility does not create an automatic right to remote work, and managers review arrangements when operational needs change.',
        'remote work, hybrid, work from home, WFH, office days, flexible location, collaboration hours, overseas working',
        'NovaTech Remote and Hybrid Work Policy (Synthetic)', 'HR'
) AS seed
WHERE @novatech_seed_lock = 1
  AND NOT EXISTS (
      SELECT 1 FROM company_knowledge AS existing
      WHERE existing.category = seed.category
        AND existing.title = seed.title
        AND existing.source_name = seed.source_name
  );

COMMIT;
SELECT RELEASE_LOCK('chatbot_db.novatech_knowledge_seed_001') AS seed_lock_released;
